+# Implementation Plan: Rental Module
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Summary
+One module `src/rental.ts` (pure helpers + `createRentalService`), re-exported from `src/index.ts`. State in closures/Maps. Tests in `test/rental.test.ts` with `node:test`, run by Node's built-in TypeScript type stripping (no dependency).
+
+## Constitution Check (before and after design)
+- I No runtime deps: pass (none added).
+- II Strict TS/ESM: pass; no `any`, tsconfig unchanged.
+- III Tests: pass; deterministic, no clock/randomness (sequential booking ids).
+- IV Explicit rules: pass; each rule a named function (`parsePeriod`, `overlaps`); season rule not guessed (assumption in spec).
+- V Simplicity: pass; one file, plain Maps.
+
+## Design
+- `parseMidnightUtc(s)`: regex `^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}T00:00:00(\.0+)?Z$`, then `Date.parse` and round-trip check of the date; returns ms.
+- days = (end - start) / 86_400_000, must be integer ≥ 1 (UTC has no DST).
+- total = days × dailyPrice (integers; checked safe).
+- overlap: `aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd`, per item.
+- Errors: plain `Error` with message (RangeError for validation).
+- Tests import `../src/index.ts` (type stripping); `src/` itself has no relative imports.
