+# Feature Specification: Rental Module
+
+**Feature Branch**: `001-rental-module`
+**Created**: 2026-11-11
+**Status**: Draft
+**Input**: User description: "Rental module for the booking desk: createRentalService() with addEquipment, quote and book; whole-day UTC periods, integer euro cents, no overlapping bookings of the same item; cancellation not yet implemented."
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*
+
+### User Story 1 - Register rental equipment (Priority: P1)
+
+The desk registers boards and sails, each with an id, a kind (board or sail) and a price per day.
+
+**Why this priority**: Nothing can be quoted or booked without equipment.
+
+**Independent Test**: Add an item, then quote it; an unknown id is refused.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** an empty desk, **When** a board `b1` at 2500 cents/day is added, **Then** it can be quoted.
+2. **Given** an item with id `b1`, **When** another item with id `b1` is added, **Then** it is refused.
+3. **Given** an item with a kind other than board/sail, a blank id, or a price that is not a non-negative integer, **When** it is added, **Then** it is refused.
+
+---
+
+### User Story 2 - Quote a rental (Priority: P1)
+
+The desk asks what renting an item for a period costs.
+
+**Independent Test**: Quote 3 days of a 2500-cent item: total 7500.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** item `b1` at 2500 cents/day, **When** quoting 2027-06-01T00:00:00Z to 2027-06-04T00:00:00Z, **Then** total is 7500 and itemId, start, end are echoed.
+2. **Given** an unknown item, **When** quoting, **Then** an error is thrown.
+3. **Given** a period not on midnight UTC, not ISO-8601 UTC, empty or reversed, **When** quoting, **Then** an error is thrown.
+
+---
+
+### User Story 3 - Book a rental (Priority: P1)
+
+The desk books an item for a period and gets a booking with an id and the total.
+
+**Independent Test**: Book, then book an overlapping period: second is refused.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** a free item, **When** booked, **Then** a booking with a unique id and the quoted total is returned.
+2. **Given** a booking for June 1–4, **When** the same item is booked June 3–6, **Then** an error is thrown and nothing is stored.
+3. **Given** a booking for June 1–4, **When** the same item is booked June 4–6 (back to back), **Then** it succeeds.
+4. **Given** a booking of item `b1`, **When** another item is booked for the same period, **Then** it succeeds.
+
+### Edge Cases
+
+- Period ending exactly where another starts does not overlap.
+- Quote does not reserve anything; a quote never fails because of existing bookings.
+- A failed booking leaves no trace.
+- Times with an offset (e.g. `+02:00`) are refused, even if equal to midnight UTC.
+
+## Requirements *(mandatory)*
+
+### Functional Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: `createRentalService()` is exported from `src/index.ts` and returns an independent in-memory service each call.
+- **FR-002**: `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })` registers an item; kind is `'board'` or `'sail'`; duplicate ids, blank ids, invalid kinds and prices that are not non-negative integer cents are refused.
+- **FR-003**: `quote({ itemId, start, end })` returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }` with total = number of days × dailyPrice, in integer euro cents.
+- **FR-004**: `book(request)` returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }` with a unique booking id.
+- **FR-005**: Times are ISO-8601 UTC strings; a period starts and ends at midnight UTC, `end` being the start of the day after the last day, and covers at least one day.
+- **FR-006**: `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a disallowed period; `book` also throws when the item has an overlapping booking.
+- **FR-007**: Periods are half-open: back-to-back bookings of the same item do not overlap.
+- **FR-008**: Cancellation is out of scope; the 24-hour refund policy is not implemented here.
+
+### Key Entities
+
+- **Equipment item**: id, kind (board | sail), daily price in cents.
+- **Rental period**: start and end, midnight UTC, whole days.
+- **Booking**: id, item, period, total.
+
+## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*
+
+### Measurable Outcomes
+
+- **SC-001**: Every quote equals days × daily price exactly, with no fractional cents.
+- **SC-002**: No two bookings of the same item ever overlap.
+- **SC-003**: Every disallowed request is refused with an error and changes nothing.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- `dailyPrice` is in euro cents (rule 1); the same price applies to every day.
+- The April–October season, student/visitor differences and capacity are not part of the stated rules; they are not enforced here (to be settled in a later request).
+- Accepted time format: `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00(.000)Z`; output echoes the input strings.
+- Booking ids are generated by the service (sequential counter, no clock or randomness needed).
+- Cancellation will come later; bookings keep what it will need (start, total).
